DECISION
AR-H110 is POSITIVE WITH A SINGLE-SENSOR FAST-PATH FAILURE.

Supported synthetically:

- persistence-only authority misses short real anomalies;
- one-sensor fast override destroys normal accuracy;
- two ordinary sensors still produce excessive false urgency;
- independent typed urgency corroboration preserves normal hierarchy while adding transient sensitivity;
- the dual-timescale policy improves both persistent and brief anomaly handling;
- fast false events remain transient rather than rewriting slow context.

Not demonstrated:

- learned urgency anchors;
- variable anomaly stakes;
- adversarial urgent-signal corruption;
- event-wave implementation;
- many anomaly types;
- interaction with resource scarcity.

